## 22. Definition of Done

A feature is **Done** only if all are true:
1. Implemented per PRD requirement and acceptance criteria, UI **and** backend **and** persistence.
2. Works in the browser end-to-end (manually or via E2E) — no console errors/warnings in the flow.
3. Input validated (client + server); errors handled with the standard envelope and friendly UI messages.
4. Loading/empty/error states exist; responsive at 360/768/1280 px; keyboard accessible.
5. Unit/integration tests written and passing; `npm run lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build` all pass.
6. No secrets in code or logs; no placeholder controls; no unused code.
7. Docs updated (`README`, `ARCHITECTURE` if contracts changed, `docs/PROGRESS.md`).

The **project** is Done when: all PRD Must items pass their acceptance criteria; PRD §22 success metrics that are measurable by you (coverage, Lighthouse, audit, 20 PDF exports) are recorded with results; `docs/PROGRESS.md` honestly lists any Should/Could items not delivered and any known issues; the README lets a new developer run the app from a clean clone in ≤ 10 minutes with `AI_PROVIDER=mock`.

## 23. Working Protocol (how to run each phase)

1. **Plan** — restate the phase tasks in `docs/PROGRESS.md`.
2. **Build** — smallest vertical slice first (DB → API → UI), commit often.
3. **Verify** — run tests; run the app; click through the flows in a browser; fix issues.
4. **Reflect** — log deviations/known issues; update docs.
5. **Gate** — check the Definition of Done; only then start the next phase.

If blocked by something only the human can provide (API key, DB URI, deployment credentials): continue with the mock/local alternative, record the exact blocker and what the human must do in `docs/PROGRESS.md`, and move on.